{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Abu Dawud","section":{"28":{"eng-name":"Foods (Kitab Al-At'imah)","ara-name":"كتاب الأطعمة"}},"section_detail":{"28":{"hadithnumber_first":3736,"hadithnumber_last":3854,"arabicnumber_first":3736,"arabicnumber_last":3854}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":3791,"arabicnumber":3791,"text":"Rapporté par Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه : J’étais un jeune garçon. J’ai chassé un lièvre et je l’ai rôti. Abu Talha a envoyé sa bosse par mon intermédiaire au Prophète ﷺ, alors je la lui ai apportée et il l’a acceptée","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Bukhari (2572) Sahih Muslim (1953)"}],"reference":{"book":28,"hadith":56},"chapter":{"id":27,"ara-name":"باب فِي أَكْلِ الأَرْنَبِ","eng-name":"Regarding eating rabbit","isFirstHadith":true}}]}